            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of verapamil on the functional status of thrombocytes in patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of 20 anginal patients demonstrated signs of platelet hyperreactivity: increased platelet aggregation, increased mobilization of Ca2+ from platelet membranes, and increased production of malonic dialdehyde. A short-term treatment with isoptin-120 (360 mg daily) produced a considerable drop in those parameters. It is suggested that the drug's basic effect is due to the inhibition of intracellular calcium redistribution in the platelets of coronary patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
